    "body": "REVIEW BLOCKER | PR #433, exact HEAD c6fbeeeab33dc67e01b7e27e6bc823c22c75d0b3\n\nThe user-authored exact copy for all five profiles matches the approved prompt; checked all affected startup/modal layers and 6 identical Web/docs pairs (ui-boot.js keeps unrelated pre-existing byte drift). Both exact-HEAD Actions passed. The two old Zoomer battle label mismatches are outside the changed startup/modal scope.\n\nOne blocking regression: tools/test_stage7_essence_modal.py was rewritten and removed earlier executable contract assertions while leaving START_BLOCK_SHA256 defined but **unused**. The previous test guarded actual start markup integrity, modal role/aria-labelledby/aria-describedby IDs, Escape/Tab/focus restoration, focus trap binding and modal open/close public API. The new test mainly verifies exact copy and only checks one aria-label plus getStage7EssenceCopy. This violates the task's explicit rule not to weaken tests, despite the runtime code itself remaining intact.\n\nCodex: update THIS SAME branch and Draft PR. Retain all new literal-copy and 5-profile tests, AND restore meaningful executed regressions for (1) actual start markup hash / required IDs & labels (update the hash only if justified by exact approved static copy change); (2) modal role, both valid ARIA targets, Escape, Tab focus trap, restored focus, open and close public APIs and their actual event paths; (3) correct one-time resource tags / load order. Prefer DOM-executed assertions for behavior, not only token presence; preserve available static invariants at minimum. Do not change any user-authored text or game mechanics to fix tests, and do not rewrite historical frozen documents. Re-run focused tests, node syntax, diff check, mirror parity, and exact-new-HEAD CI. Mobile 375x667/320x480 visual evidence is still missing, so record as pending user Safari if the approved Codex Browser cannot select those viewports. Return updated HEAD; do NOT merge or claim Safari PASS.",
